  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY NIGHT THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 122 PM MDT Mon Jul 27 2026\n\nWednesday will likely be a repeat performance of Tuesday, with \nnumerous to scattered thunderstorms, capable of producing heavy rain, \nover all of the region. QPF guidance shows a better chance of \nheavier precip over a good part of the region as compared to \nTuesday. Flash flooding threat may be exacerbated on Wednesday if \nflash flood prone areas see heavy rain on Tuesday. \n\nThursday...\n\nScattered to likely showers are expected over the mountains with only \nisolated to scattered storms over the plains. Temps will warm up a \nbit with 90s to L100s over the plains.\n\nFriday...\n\nSimilar temps to Thursday, but less pops regionwide.\n\nWeekend...\n\nDrier and hot, but not as hot as today or yesterday.\n\nLooking a bit farther out...deterministic guidance hints at a \nCanadian front trying to push into the region for next Tuesday-\nish. Both EC and GFS show this solution, but GFS is much more \namplified while EC has more of a glancing blow. Lets hope! \n\\/Hodanish",
